# Binary assets must never have their line endings "fixed".
#
# Git auto-detects most of these, and auto-detection is exactly the kind of
# thing that works until it does not — a decoder or a model corrupted by CRLF
# translation fails at runtime, in the browser, with nothing pointing at the
# commit that did it. This says so explicitly instead.
#
# The Draco decoder is the immediate reason: public/draco/draco_decoder.wasm is
# the one file in the project whose corruption would break every compressed GLB
# at once.

*.wasm   binary
*.glb    binary
*.gltf   binary
*.ktx2   binary
*.basis  binary
*.hdr    binary
*.exr    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.webp   binary
*.mp3    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.wav    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
